## Research Findings (2026-01-18)

### Offset Pagination is Fragile
The current bead uses OFFSET/LIMIT which has issues:
- Slow for large offsets (DB scans all skipped rows)
- Race conditions if data changes during backfill

### Better Approach: Cursor-based
```typescript
let lastId: string | null = null;
while (true) {
  const batch = await db
    .select()
    .from(schema.tasks)
    .where(
      and(
        isNull(schema.tasks.embedding),
        lastId ? gt(schema.tasks.id, lastId) : undefined
      )
    )
    .orderBy(schema.tasks.id)
    .limit(BATCH_SIZE);

  if (batch.length === 0) break;
  lastId = batch[batch.length - 1].id;
  // Process batch...
}
```

### Rate Limit Delay
- Current 1-second delay is too conservative
- Reduce to 100-200ms between batches
- Add exponential backoff only on 429 errors

### Progress Tracking
```typescript
console.log(`Processed ${processed}/${total} (${(processed/total*100).toFixed(1)}%)`);
```

